        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"9\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"11\") (name \"SCK\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"RST\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"~{RESET}/PB5\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"~{RESET}/PB5\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U2\") (value \"ATtiny45-20P\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U3\") (value \"ATtiny13V-10S\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCUs are populated, they can drive shared GPIO nets simultaneously. Conflicting output states can cause incorrect fan control and excessive current or damage to the MCU output pins.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist places two different ATtiny MCUs on the same control nets, with no indication that they are mutually exclusive. This is unsafe if both are populated; if they are intended alternatives, the design files do not make that population constraint explicit."
}

